  "provenance": "Builder-authored AI development expectations frozen before method changes. Case-informed diagnostic sample, not independent human judgement or an accuracy estimate. Human validation deferred, zero human judgements.",
  "policy": [
    "Both methods use identical eligible IDs/exclusion counts on the same 20 cases. No record, source attribution, date or M001 changes. No first-stage actions/outcomes/identity/figures.",
    "Distinguish fuel, petrochemical inputs/packaging, natural fats/oils, edible/vegetable oils and specific named oil inputs. Generic natural fats/oils do not establish edible use or a particular plant. Copra is dried coconut kernel, not coconut oil or a fuel.",
    "Paper/cardboard words have explicit Kao pressure evidence; do not infer pulp. Specific petrochemical packaging requests are not satisfied by generic packaging alone.",
    "Nestle oil-linked distribution/packaging evidence can be a qualified related cost comparison, never proof of diesel or another exact fuel/material. No fuel comparison with edible/natural oils or petrochemical material solely via oil.",
    "Bare oil has no safe type. Ask for a material clarification; other clearly named pressures may still produce partial results. Negation, role and cost direction stay conservative.",
    "Report missing useful cases, forbidden/unexpected results, named versus related support, and every historical target regression. Do not tune labels or cases after rankings."
  ],
  "source_checks": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.nestle.com/media/pressreleases/allpressreleases/half-year-results2011",
      "locator": "Nestle Waters final bullet; 10 August 2011",
      "finding": "Source reports oil-related distribution and packaging costs, without naming diesel. Treat fuel link as broader cost evidence, not exact-input support."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://marico.com/investorspdf/Information_Update_April_30_2021.pdf",
      "locator": "Update printed pp. 4 and 6, input/pricing and footnote (a); 30 April 2021",
